{"name":"Fireplace Mantel","hex":"#847c70","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fireplace","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An open hearth for holding a fire at the base of a chimney."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fireplace"},{"term":"mantel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The shelf above a fireplace which may be also a structural support for the masonry of the chimney.","A maneuver to surmount a ledge, involving pushing down on the ledge to bring up the body."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To surmount a ledge by pushing down on the ledge to bring up the body."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mantel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fireplace mantel","blocks":[{"text":"A fireplace mantel or mantelpiece, also known as a chimneypiece, originated in medieval times as a hood that projected over a fire grate to catch the smoke. The term has evolved to include the decorative framework around the fireplace, and can include elaborate designs extending to the ceiling. Mantelpiece is now the general term for the jambs, mantel shelf, and external accessories of a fireplace. For many centuries, the chimneypiece was the most ornamental and most artistic feature of a room, but as fireplaces have become smaller, and modern methods of heating have been introduced, its artistic as well as its practical significance has lessened."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Arlington_House_-_State_Dining_Room_-_fireplace_mantel_-_2011.jpg/330px-Arlington_House_-_State_Dining_Room_-_fireplace_mantel_-_2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fireplace_mantel","wikidata":"Q4327778"},{"title":"Fireplace","blocks":[{"text":"A fireplace or hearth is a structure made of brick, stone or metal designed to contain a fire. Fireplaces are used to heat a room or dwelling and also for the relaxing ambiance they create. Modern fireplaces vary in heat efficiency, depending on the design."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Open_fireplace_with_icon.jpg/330px-Open_fireplace_with_icon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fireplace","wikidata":"Q188669"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Chimneypiece_MET_SF1972_276_2.jpg/500px-Chimneypiece_MET_SF1972_276_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Chimneypiece_MET_SF1972_276_2.jpg/1280px-Chimneypiece_MET_SF1972_276_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Chimneypiece_MET_SF1972_276_2.jpg/500px-Chimneypiece_MET_SF1972_276_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Parisian chimneypiece, circa 1775–1785, Carrara marble with gilt bronze, height: .mw-parser-output .frac{white-space:nowrap}.mw-parser-output .frac .num,.mw-parser-output .frac .den{font-size:80%;line-height:0;vertical-align:super}.mw-parser-output .frac .den{vertical-align:sub}.mw-parser-output .sr-only{border:0;clip:rect(0,0,0,0);clip-path:polygon(0px 0px,0px 0px,0px 0px);height:1px;margin:-1px;overflow:hidden;padding:0;position:absolute;width:1px}111.4 cm (43+3⁄4 in), width: 169.5 cm (66+3⁄4 in), depth: 41.9 cm (16+1⁄2 in), Metropolitan Museum of Art (New York City)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChimneypiece_MET_SF1972_276_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Fireplace_and_over_mantel.jpg/500px-Fireplace_and_over_mantel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Fireplace_and_over_mantel.jpg/1280px-Fireplace_and_over_mantel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia